  1 passed Book a demo FIT CHECK Is this the right email testing tool?  It is built for tests that need to read real email in CI. Strong fit when Your signup, reset or invite tests currently sleep, scrape Gmail, or share one QA mailbox. Your app sends through SES, Postmark, Resend or an auth provider, and you want to test the real message end to end. Security will not allow a public disposable-mail domain. Not the best fit when You only need to catch mail your app sends to localhost. A local SMTP catcher does that job. You need to send email, test SMS, or receive phone verification codes. Email Testing receives mail only. You want a public inbox anyone can read. Every address here is private to your workspace. Book a demo Read the docs PRICING A free plan.  Paid plans from $19 a month. Testing is its own plan, on the same subscription as monitoring. Add it to any monitoring plan, Free included. Free $0 1 email domain 3 webhook inboxes 300 stored events / mo 3-day event history Book a demo Developer $19 / mo 1 email domain 10 webhook inboxes 3,000 stored events / mo 7-day event history Book a demo Team $79 / mo 3 email domains Your own domain (custom MX) 100 webhook inboxes 100,000 stored events / mo 30-day event history Book a demo Business $149 / mo 10 email domains Your own domain (custom MX) 500 webhook inboxes 300,000 stored events / mo 90-day event history Book a demo Enterprise: unlimited domains, inboxes and events, 365-day history, custom pricing. Stored events count email and webhook together. Annual billing: two months free. FAQ Frequently asked questions  Addresses, codes, privacy and pricing. How do I test OTP emails in Playwright? + Use a fresh address per run, such as signup-${Date.now()}@your-domain , trigger the email, and call the wait endpoint for that address. The response includes the extracted code; fill it into your form. How do I test magic links? + Same flow: wait for the message, then page.goto the extracted link. No HTML parsing in your test. Do I have to create an inbox before sending to it? + No. Every address at your private domain already exists. Use any string before the @. What happens if the email never arrives? + The wait call returns HTTP 408 WAIT_TIMEOUT after your timeout (default 30 s, maximum 120 s). It never returns an empty success. Open the domain in the dashboard to see whether anything arrived for that address. Is it private, or a public disposable inbox? + Private. Each workspace gets its own domain, and only that workspace can read its mail. Can I use my own domain? + On Team and above, yes: add your domain, point its MX record at DevHelm, and verify it. Is it free? What does it cost? + There is a free plan: 1 domain, 300 stored events a month and 3 days of history. Paid plans are $19, $79 and $149 per month, and annual billing gets two months free. Book a demo Stop reading the QA Gmail.  Wait for the email. The beta is open by invitation. Book a 30-minute demo and we'll set up your workspace. TERMINAL $ curl -sS -X POST https://api.devhelm.io/api/v1/email/wait \
